<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<speak version="1.1" xml:lang="en-US">
  <voice name="en-US-AndrewNeural">
    <prosody rate="+0%">
      <p id="scene-01">
        <s>Hi! This is StatePort — a place on your own computer where the work you do with AI can live.</s>
        <break time="450ms"/>
        <s>Let me show you what that means, in about a minute.</s>
      </p>
      <p id="scene-02">
        <s>This is one of those projects.</s>
        <break time="450ms"/>
        <s>Instead of hiding inside a chat, it keeps its own notes: what the goal is, what happened so far, and what needs your attention next.</s>
      </p>
      <p id="scene-03">
        <s>You can still chat with an AI helper — here it is called a coding agent.</s>
        <break time="450ms"/>
        <s>StatePort runs it through a managed workspace on your machine.</s>
        <s>A job can use a sandbox or container when you configure one.</s>
        <s>The agent gets bounded tools and permissions, and asks before anything important changes.</s>
      </p>
      <p id="scene-04">
        <s>This page is the project's memory: what is finished, what is still being checked, and what is only an experiment — so you know what to trust.</s>
      </p>
      <p id="scene-05">
        <s>And yes — the same project reads fine on your phone.</s>
      </p>
      <p id="scene-06">
        <s>One honest note: this is a preview from my own computer.</s>
        <break time="450ms"/>
        <s>StatePort is in private alpha, works with one AI coding tool so far, and can't be downloaded yet.</s>
        <s>The idea is simple: give AI work a real home, keep you in charge, and keep what's yours, yours.</s>
      </p>
    </prosody>
  </voice>
</speak>
